meta {
  name: 01_ConnectionsActivityLog
  seq: 1
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Scenario: Giving and removing access is recorded in the connections activity log

    Given the delegator has no connection to the receiver
    And the delegator makes the receiver a rightholder
    And the delegator gives the receiver an access package
    When the delegator reads the log of access it has given
    Then the role assignment and the access package are recorded as created
    And the receiver sees the same events in the log of access it has received
    And the log can be narrowed to one activity type
    And the filter values list the receiver
    And the log is paginated newest first
    And the next page continues without overlap
    And an outsider cannot read the delegator's log
    And the receiver cannot read the delegator's log either
    And the to-others scope reads the access given
    But the to-others scope does not read the access received
    When the delegator removes the connection to the receiver
    Then the removal of the role assignment and the access package is recorded
}
